BT 40.00 680.00 Td (1. Executive Summary: Why Aligning Geographic Data is Hard) Tj ET
/F1 9.5 Tf
BT 40.00 662.00 Td (In modern 3D graphics, visual effects, and digital twin simulation, developers frequently combine multiple) Tj ET
BT 40.00 649.00 Td (distinct data sources from Google Maps and GIS providers into a single interactive 3D viewport. At first glance,) Tj ET
BT 40.00 636.00 Td (one might assume that everything with a GPS coordinate naturally lines up. In practice, they violently clash:) Tj ET
BT 40.00 623.00 Td (- 3D Photorealistic Tiles arrive as continuous, textured geometric meshes measured from the center of the Earth.) Tj ET
BT 40.00 610.00 Td (- 2D Roadmaps & Cadastral Parcels arrive as flat, 2D curves projected via Web Mercator without intrinsic depth.) Tj ET
BT 40.00 597.00 Td (- Elevation services report heights above sea level, while GPS satellites report heights above a mathematical oval.) Tj ET
BT 40.00 584.00 Td (Without a disciplined mathematical architecture, cars float 30 meters above streets, roads pierce through tunnels,) Tj ET
BT 40.00 571.00 Td (and camera viewports jitter uncontrollably due to 32-bit floating-point precision exhaustion.) Tj ET
/F2 13 Tf
BT 40.00 548.00 Td (2. The Layman's Analogy: The 'Skin & Bones' Architecture) Tj ET
/F1 9.5 Tf
/F1 9.5 Tf
