BT 40.00 505.00 Td (A. The Photographic 'Skin' \(Google 3D Photorealistic Tiles & Cesium\):) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 492.50 Td (   Think of 3D map tiles as the outer skin. They look stunning, photorealistic, and complete. However, the computer) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 480.00 Td (   has no clue what anything is. To the computer, a tree, an asphalt lane, a fire hydrant, and a skyscraper are all just) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 467.50 Td (   one continuous soup of millions of colored triangles. You cannot ask the skin 'where does lane 2 turn left?'.) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 455.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.150 0.350 0.750 rg
BT 40.00 442.50 Td (B. The Semantic 'Bones' \(Google 2D Vector Roadmap, OpenStreetMap, Overture Maps\):) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 430.00 Td (   Vector data is the skeleton. It consists of mathematical polylines, legal speed limits, lane boundaries, cadastral) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 417.50 Td (   property parcels, and building footprints. It knows exactly what each element is, but it has no 3D photographic volume.) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 405.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.150 0.350 0.750 rg
BT 40.00 392.50 Td (C. The Co-Registration Fusion:) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 380.00 Td (   Scratchbox fuses the 'Skin' and 'Bones' together onto a shared mathematical skeleton. The vector skeleton drives vehicle) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 367.50 Td (   pathfinding, curb bevels, and bridge excavation, while the photographic skin provides VFX-grade visual fidelity.) Tj ET
