BT 40.00 715.00 Td (3. The Elevation Riddle: Why Elevation Coordinates Don't Naturally Match) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 699.00 Td (Elevation is where most multi-source 3D applications fail. The fundamental confusion arises because Earth is not) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 687.00 Td (a smooth sphere, nor is it a simple geometric oval. It is an irregular potato shaped by variations in Earth's gravity field.) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 675.00 Td (Consequently, geospatial science defines two completely distinct measurements of height:) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 663.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.0 Tf
0.150 0.350 0.750 rg
BT 40.00 651.00 Td (1. Ellipsoidal Height \(h\): Measured by GPS satellites, Google 3D Tiles, and Cesium. This is the pure geometric) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 639.00 Td (   distance in meters from the mathematical WGS-84 reference ellipsoid.) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 627.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.0 Tf
0.150 0.350 0.750 rg
BT 40.00 615.00 Td (2. Orthometric Height \(H\): Measured by surveyors, Mean Sea Level \(MSL\), and Google 2D Roadmaps. This is the height) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 603.00 Td (   above where calm sea water would sit under Earth's actual gravitational field \(the Geoid\).) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 591.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.800 0.200 0.100 rg
BT 40.00 579.00 Td (The difference between them is the Geoid Undulation \(N\):   h = H + N) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 567.00 Td (In New York City, N is approx. -31.5 meters. In Singapore, N is +14.0 meters. If a developer pastes vector road data) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 555.00 Td (directly into 3D photogrammetric tiles without geoid undulation compensation, the road will either hover 31 meters) Tj ET
/F1 8.8 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 543.00 Td (in mid-air or plunge 31 meters beneath the pavement. Scratchbox dynamically resolves N everywhere on Earth.) Tj ET
0.100 0.100 0.100 rg
/F2 12 Tf
BT 40.00 523.00 Td (4. The 2-Layer Canonical Architecture \(Rigorously Audited\)) Tj ET
/F1 9.0 Tf
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 507.00 Td (A critical question arose during system architecture: Should we mandate WGS-84 coordinates on everything in the engine?) Tj ET
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 495.00 Td (A ruthless first-principles critical thinking audit revealed that mandating GPS coordinates on everything is a catastrophic anti-pattern:) Tj ET
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 483.00 Td (- It violates the 'Alien Planet Test' \(ADA Pillar 1\): An alien rover or fictional starship cannot have GPS coordinates on Earth.) Tj ET
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 471.00 Td (- It causes the 'Null Island' disaster: Developers default non-geolocated assets to \(0,0\), dropping them off the coast of Ghana.) Tj ET
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 459.00 Td (- It forces CAD/character artists to configure GIS projections just to sculpt a humanoid or coffee cup.) Tj ET
/F1 8.7 Tf
0.200 0.200 0.200 rg
BT 40.00 447.00 Td () Tj ET
/F2 9.2 Tf
0.100 0.100 0.100 rg
